{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":2846234,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,4]],"date-time":"2024-09-04T18:43:51Z","timestamp":1725475431403},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"WORLD SCIENTIFIC","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2001,4]]},"DOI":"10.1142\/9789812794598_0001","type":"proceedings-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2010,5,24]],"date-time":"2010-05-24T00:05:15Z","timestamp":1274659515000},"page":"1-32","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["RETURN TO EQUILIBRIUM IN CLASSICAL AND QUANTUM SYSTEMS"],"prefix":"10.1142","author":[{"given":"CARLANGELO","family":"LIVERANI","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Dipartimento di Matematica, II universit\u00e0 di Roma (Tor Vergata), via Della Ricerca Scientifica, 00133 Roma, Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2011,11,21]]},"event":{"name":"Proceedings of the Bologna APTEX International Conference","location":"Bologna, Italy"},"container-title":["Long Time Behaviour of Classical and Quantum Systems"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2017,7,12]],"date-time":"2017-07-12T18:44:55Z","timestamp":1499885095000},"score":28.690231,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/www.worldscientific.com\/doi\/abs\/10.1142\/9789812794598_0001"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2001,4]]},"references-count":0,"alternative-id":["10.1142\/9789812794598_0001","10.1142\/4640"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1142\/9789812794598_0001","published":{"date-parts":[[2001,4]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,12]],"date-time":"2026-06-12T16:05:45Z","timestamp":1781280345627,"version":"3.54.1"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,19]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,19]],"date-time":"2025-07-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1752883200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Time-series forecasting is vital across sectors such as finance, energy, and environmental science, where accurate future predictions drive informed decision-making. Traditional statistical methods and deep learning models like LSTM and Transformers, while effective, often struggle with high-dimensional data and long-term dependencies. In this paper, we propose a hybrid quantum-classical model that utilizes Parameterized Quantum Circuits (PQCs) to capture complex temporal patterns in multivariate time-series data. Our architecture integrates a classical encoder, a quantum variational processor, and a classical decoder, trained end-to-end using gradient-based optimization. Experiments conducted on benchmark datasets\u2014electricity load, stock prices, and weather forecasting\u2014demonstrate that the hybrid model consistently outperforms classical baselines in terms of Mean Squared Error (MSE), Mean Absolute Error (MAE), and R\u00b2 score. Robustness analysis confirms the model\u2019s resilience to moderate quantum noise, while an ablation study highlights the performance gain from quantum components. This work showcases the potential of hybrid quantum-classical approaches on Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum (NISQ) devices and lays a foundation for scalable, real-world quantum machine learning applications.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.36227\/techrxiv.175295886.67877890\/v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,19]],"date-time":"2025-07-19T21:01:12Z","timestamp":1752958872000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Optimizing Hybrid\u00a0Quantum-Classical Models Using Parameterized Quantum Circuits for Time-Series\u00a0Forecasting"],"prefix":"10.36227","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0008-3908-3735","authenticated-orcid":false,"g